  "slug": "anthrocon",
  "name": "Anthrocon",
  "shortName": null,
  "description": "Anthrocon is an annual furry convention and one of the largest in the world, held at the David L. Lawrence Convention Center in Pittsburgh, Pennsylvania, since 2006. It began in 1997 as Albany AnthroCon in Albany, New York, with an estimated 300 attendees, then moved to Valley Forge in 1999 and Philadelphia in 2001. It is run by Anthrocon, Inc., a Pennsylvania not-for-profit, and has been chaired since 1999 by Dr. Samuel Conway, known as Uncle Kage. Attendance reached 20,618 in 2026, its twentieth year in Pittsburgh, when the city declared July 1 \"Anthrocon Day\". Each year it partners with a local Pennsylvania charity, and its mascot is Anthrocat.",
